The [product] 's are great but you really don't need to get the [product]. they are harder to drive. they'll be technically superior in rather subtle ways. I think you're better off getting the [impedance] and be able to use it directly with a phone or computer if you need to. I use a dac/amp 80% of the time, but still like to have equipment that works with my phone.

I really like the [brand] [model]’s. I actually use a lower end, closed version of them in my video conferencing studio. I only need them for voice , and most peopel are talking into crap equipment so the $40 version of them are honestly more than enough. I picked them because they are very light and comfortable for long term wearing. I'd like the get the [model]/[model] at some point but I don't need them. I'd recommend getting the [retailer] [model]’s over the retail version because you'll get nearly identical headphones at a lower price. I think you will be pretty happy with them as they have a relatively neutral sound so they should sound good with just about any music.

