By sound profiles I mean like how much bass, sub bass, and treble you like.   


One of the nice thing about the [device] is it has pretty high power so it will work with most hard to drive headphones. It also has very low output impedance so it will work well with very sensitive headphones. Pretty much 95% of what you might buy. probably more. The [model]s are going to be a little hard to drive with most computers and headphones. Your motherboard probably can but a good dac/amp is going to improve the sound a bit and then you know you'll be able to crank the sound. I imagine the 300 ohm thing means that it can power the [model]/[model] which are 300 ohmds and hard to drive. THe truth is it doesn;t mean that much because impedance is only part of the picture when it comes to how hard headphones are to drive. getting the DAC/AMP with give you a cleaner sound with more detail and probably more powerful and accurate bass.

