We all start somewhere. I used to be a pretty serious cuber. Now I just do it for fun when I'm bored. 

&nbsp;

Cubing is more about self improvement than trying to be better than everyone else. we all want each other and the hobby to get better. When I went to my first comp about 10 years ago I traveled hundreds of miles and didn't know anyone. I ended up sitting at a table with two of the best cubers in the country. I befriended one and he gave me tips on what to do to be better. He went on to win multiple world records. Can you imagine going to your first basketball tournament with no friends and getting pointers from a famous NBA star by accident? We're happy that people keep joining our hobby that to most people is a pop culture fad from the 80s.

